       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and, in overdose, prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nCould you tell me which of these applies?\n\n1. **It was a typo.** If you meant 3 mg, I'd suggest 2.5 mg or 5 mg, since those are the available strengths. If you meant 10 mg, I can enter that.\n2. **The dose is intentional.** This might be a specific refractory case. If so, please confirm the dose and I'll enter it. I'll add a note such as \"Dose exceeds labeled maximum \u2013 confirmed by attending\" so pharmacy and nursing can see it was deliberate.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter the order right away."
      }
